# There is one .gitignore, this file. Path-anchoring is load-bearing in places — see the notes on
# the rules that carry one.

# ─── Dependencies ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/

# ─── Build output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.next/
/out/
/build
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ─── Generated media variants ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Written by `npm run media:generate` (WP-03) and — under the default filesystem source —
# a link to the key's media library written by `npm run media:link`.
#
# NO TRAILING SLASH, and that is load-bearing rather than tidying. `/public/media/` matches
# directories ONLY, so it would not ignore the link itself: a symlink could then be committed,
# pointing at an absolute path on one machine. Everywhere else it dangles, and on Windows —
# where git has core.symlinks=false — it is checked out as a regular FILE, at which point the
# build's `mkdir public/media` fails with ENOTDIR. Without the slash this rule covers the
# directory and the link alike.
/public/media

# ─── The media library ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The derived variants every `/media/...` URL resolves to. Ignored, never committed —
# the whole point of the media seam is that a clone stays cheap. It lives INSIDE the
# repository anyway for two reasons: a path outside the root forces `turbopack.root` to be
# widened to the parent directory (Turbopack rejects symlinks that resolve outside its root),
# and `npm run media:link` can link `public/media` at it.
#
# Derived — `npm run media:generate` (WP-03) rebuilds the whole tree from the originals.

/media/
# The manifest is committed: a clean clone has no originals to read, and the committed
# manifest is what keeps one building and exporting byte-identically. The key file makes
# the key a fact of the commit rather than of the checkout (a tag checkout has no branch
# to resolve it from). Everything else under .media/ stays out.
.media/*
!.media/key
!.media/manifest.json

# ─── The originals ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `media-originals/…` — the user's drop folder, bridged into the repository by a local-only
# symlink (not committed). THE ONE THING HERE THAT IS NOT REPRODUCIBLE: it is the sole copy
# of the client's originals, so it is what a backup has to cover.
#
# Ignored for the same reason the library is — a clone has to stay cheap. The
# trailing-slash form covers the directory; the bare name covers the symlink.
/media-originals/
/media-originals

# ─── Test output ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/coverage
/test-results/
/playwright-report/
/blob-report/
/playwright/.cache/

# ─── Secrets — none belong in this repository at all ────────────────────────────
.env*
*.pem

# The deployment ssh key. A GUARD, not housekeeping: the key belongs in `~/.ssh` and nothing
# here reads it, so nothing should ever create it in this tree. A private key in a git
# history is not undone by deleting the file. The `*` covers the private key and the
# `.pub` alike.
/deploy_key*

# ─── Guard rules ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The rules below are a **guard, not housekeeping**: the intake directories they name do not
# exist yet, and these entries exist so that dropping media into that layout cannot quietly add
# camera originals to a clone.
#
# ANCHORED with leading slashes, and that is load-bearing: a bare `fonts/` matches a directory
# of that name at ANY depth and would swallow `public/fonts/` (WP-04's subsetted faces).
/fonts/
/logo/

# ─── Editor / OS noise ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.eslintcache
.cache/
.vercel/
dist/

# VS Code workspace settings (local to each developer)
.vscode/settings.json
.vscode/launch.json
.vscode/extensions.json

# Throwaway probes written while debugging — scratch, and unanchored so one is ignored
# wherever it is dropped. Paired with the same rule in .prettierignore.
*.tmp.*

# IDE-specific files
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.idea/
*.iml
.pnpm-debug.log*
